      "writtenOn": "2026-05-15T00:33:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, this is an ABI break. The ABI does not rely on the hook headers to obtain the types. It uses the DWARF from all of the .o artifacts -- including those in drivers/usb/typec/tcpm. I extracted the definition of struct tcpm_port from android/abi_gki_aarch64.stg and it is (as expected) the complete definition. If it weren\u0027t, then the symbols that you rely on for Pixel would not be stable. Here is a partial ABI definition of struct tcpm_port (I had to skip some of it since the comment becomes too long for gerrit, but be assured the whole definition is there):\n```\nstruct tcpm_port {                                                                                                                       \n      struct device* dev; // offset: 0                                                                                                       \n      struct mutex lock; // offset: 64                                                                                                       \n      struct kthread_worker* wq; // offset: 448                                                                                              \n      struct typec_capability typec_caps; // offset: 512                                                                                     \n      struct typec_port* typec_port; // offset: 1216                                                                                         \n      struct tcpc_dev* tcpc; // offset: 1280                                                                                                 \n      struct usb_role_switch* role_sw; // offset: 1344                                                                                       \n      enum typec_role vconn_role; // offset: 1408                                                                                            \n      enum typec_role pwr_role; // offset: 1440                                                                                              \n      enum typec_data_role data_role; // offset: 1472                                                                                        \n      enum typec_pwr_opmode pwr_opmode; // offset: 1504                                                                                      \n      struct usb_pd_identity partner_ident; // offset: 1536                                                                                  \n      struct typec_partner_desc partner_desc; // offset: 1728                                                                                \n      struct typec_partner* partner; // offset: 1920                                                                                         \n      enum typec_cc_status cc_req; // offset: 1984                                                                                           \n      enum typec_cc_status src_rp; // offset: 2016                                                                                           \n      enum typec_cc_status cc1; // offset: 2048                                                                                              \n      enum typec_cc_status cc2; // offset: 2080                                                                                              \n      enum typec_cc_polarity polarity; // offset: 2112                                                                                       \n      bool attached; // offset: 2144                                                                                                         \n      bool connected; // offset: 2152                                                                                                        \n      bool registered; // offset: 2160                                                                                                       \n      bool pd_supported; // offset: 2168                                                                                                     \n      enum typec_port_type port_type; // offset: 2176                                                                                        \n      bool vbus_present; // offset: 2208                                                                                                     \n      bool vbus_vsafe0v; // offset: 2216                                                                                                     \n      bool vbus_never_low; // offset: 2224                                                                                                   \n      bool vbus_source; // offset: 2232                                                                                                      \n      bool vbus_charge; // offset: 2240                                                                                                      \n      bool send_discover; // offset: 2248                                                                                                    \n      bool op_vsafe5v; // offset: 2256                                                                                                       \n      int try_role; // offset: 2272                                                                                                          \n      int try_snk_count; // offset: 2304                                                                                                     \n      int try_src_count; // offset: 2336                                                                                                     \n      enum pd_msg_request queued_message; // offset: 2368                                                                                    \n      enum tcpm_state enter_state; // offset: 2400                                                                                           \n      enum tcpm_state prev_state; // offset: 2432                                                                                            \n      enum tcpm_state state; // offset: 2464                                                                                                 \n      enum tcpm_state delayed_state; // offset: 2496                                                                                         \n      ktime_t delayed_runtime; // offset: 2560                                                                                               \n\n... (skip due to Gerrit message limitations)\n\n      bool slow_charger_loop; // offset: 34320\n      bool potential_contaminant; // offset: 34328\n      struct dentry* dentry; // offset: 34368\n      struct mutex logbuffer_lock; // offset: 34432\n      int logbuffer_head; // offset: 34816\n      int logbuffer_tail; // offset: 34848\n      u8* logbuffer[1024]; // offset: 34880\n    };\n```\n\n\u003e Is the requirement to refactor based on a technical risk (e.g., something actually dereferencing the struct) or is it to satisfy the ABI monitoring tool which is flagging the change in the underlying DWARF type? If it\u0027s just the tool, can we look into an ABI suppression rule instead of refactoring the core logic?\n\nIt is assumed that when the Pixel team defines a vendor hook with struct tcpm_port as a parameter, that it will be using that struct in the handler. Since we support updating vendor modules asynchronously from the core kernel, this means the structure must be stable. You cannot change it. Period.",
